<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64001" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχώ</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεχώ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				6652.3
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχοῦς</span> is used as
			nom. sg.); so perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχώ</span> is to be
			read rather than <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχῳ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6227
			</span></i>: nom. sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχώς</span> is
				v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ep.Je.</u>
				28
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχός</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
